{"event_type":"review","id":"10c2c98e58069f45819b603a7e5df24c0f80600653a757dec3fa1af9f5cb7f40","occurred_at":"2026-11-14T17:22:15Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d11b4f66395331eaaf4151c1ad9cbd76258e52164f9bcde806ab149afcf29f39","sha256":"d11b4f66395331eaaf4151c1ad9cbd76258e52164f9bcde806ab149afcf29f39"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1baeec6fd29b7709ed353ddae0c9308a87ccc35f33fd755a33eebc4089882e7f","sha256":"1baeec6fd29b7709ed353ddae0c9308a87ccc35f33fd755a33eebc4089882e7f"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1699e0ede6e9d91223371c0eda348d9dddf362cc60ff94be73a38df7b1ca11e0","sha256":"1699e0ede6e9d91223371c0eda348d9dddf362cc60ff94be73a38df7b1ca11e0"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6448d2a2078419a5cd81696e5028363a32b129870e9ec7808fcaff9c4d8129ba","sha256":"6448d2a2078419a5cd81696e5028363a32b129870e9ec7808fcaff9c4d8129ba"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/951832b7e10fbd27ac69112e4ab00d9ad8d9690c0e923534b0fdd606e0a755de","sha256":"951832b7e10fbd27ac69112e4ab00d9ad8d9690c0e923534b0fdd606e0a755de"}],"attempt_id":"a03467887d70b6b2412bb7384031a52d998ce2f4174a7e5e64642ff974167ade:0:1","base":"eec1e5a4a3dcf7588e67bbb39239b3b1d3924404","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"ac9daf5805824fd067cfe268792ff95504863120","body":"**Settle a leg as unknown when its address report records unknown usage.**\n\n`report.usage` is an additive total. `account()` in `src/ops/review/address.ts` adds each dispatch's `result.usage` to it, whether or not the provider measured that usage. An unmeasured dispatch can therefore add zero to `report.usage`. The same dispatch is recorded as an unknown observation in `usageLedger`, and `finish()` exposes that ledger as `report.usageSummary`.\n\n`src/ops/review/addressMany.ts` reads only `report.usage`. Line 664 marks a leg `known` when that total normalizes. Lines 699-711 then settle the leg as a known token amount. The reservation is released even though provider spend is unknown. With `maxTokens=100`, `tokensPerPr=100` and concurrency 1, a later PR can then be admitted beyond the requested budget.\n\nBefore settling a leg as known, check the address report's `usageSummary` for unknown observations. When that summary contains any, settle the leg through the existing unknown-usage path at lines 713 and 724.","id":"4a911f96b0e9e31c87401c7ed36e5612a0a31b087a194c670f91fda181ab5d23","intervals":[[664,664]],"path":"src/ops/review/addressMany.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Settle a leg as unknown when its address report records unknown usage."}],"head":"7a5def0d43ef51bd4ed873fe4e1b608f8ba74d8f","head_tree":"ff441c47f135816927d2c105b0555b66502df3d8","input_scope":[{"blob":"ac9daf5805824fd067cfe268792ff95504863120","intervals":[[1,904]],"path":"src/ops/review/addressMany.ts"},{"blob":"e23e32e8526fcb4f0fb9dab7d38765d551e14881","intervals":[[1,67]],"path":"src/ops/review/record.ts"}],"job_id":"a03467887d70b6b2412bb7384031a52d998ce2f4174a7e5e64642ff974167ade:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"ac9daf5805824fd067cfe268792ff95504863120","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/review/addressMany.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"e23e32e8526fcb4f0fb9dab7d38765d551e14881","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/review/record.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"ac9daf5805824fd067cfe268792ff95504863120","intervals":[[7,7],[87,90],[95,95],[114,114],